            <ArticleTitle>An Elderly Man with a Swollen Knee,Significant Ecchymosis, and Minimal Knee Pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-100</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 72-year-old man presents with left knee pain and swelling over several days. The pain and swelling started after he felt a &quot;pop&quot; when bending to pick up an object off the floor. His past medical history is significant for type 2 diabetes mellitus. Physical exam revealed significant ecchymosis on the anterolateral aspect of the thigh. There was a minimal amount pain upon knee flexion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
